  "tagline": "Lucene-inspired full-text search library in Rust, the engine under Quickwit and ParadeDB.",
  "description": "Tantivy is a full-text search engine library written in Rust and modeled on Lucene's architecture: segment-based inverted indexes, BM25 scoring, phrase and fuzzy queries, faceting, columnar 'fast fields' for aggregations and JSON fields. It starts quickly, uses memory efficiently and often outperforms Lucene in benchmarks. It is maintained by the Quickwit team (part of Datadog since 2025) and embedded by Quickwit, ParadeDB's pg_search and many Rust applications, with Python bindings via tantivy-py. It is a library: you bring the server, replication and distribution.",
